To me, at least "deception" is intentionally acting in a way that causes the
listener to believe something you know not to be true; "lying" is actually
saying something you know not to be true (with the intent of deception);
"asshole" is a value judgement, not directly related to either of the above.
:)

Also, weirdly, I refuse to lie, but have no qualms about deception in
general.

